# Desktop entry for the Linux GUI. The basename MUST equal the Wayland
# app_id set in crates/eidola-gui/src/lib.rs (`APP_ID`) — that equality is
# how GNOME/KDE associate our windows with this entry (name in Alt-Tab and
# the shell, icon, dock pinning).
#
# The Icon key names a themed icon (`tech.m6i.Eidola.{svg,png}` under
# share/icons/hicolor/...) that does not exist yet — shipping the reference
# is harmless (shells fall back to a generic icon) and it lights up the
# moment a real brand asset lands. See AGENTS.md → Linux.
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Eidola
Comment=A quiet page for thinking with a machine — private by construction
Exec=eidola-gui %U
Icon=tech.m6i.Eidola
Terminal=false
Categories=Utility;Network;
Keywords=AI;chat;private;confidential;
